Purpose: Install extensions listed in extensions/preinstalled.toml via an external-provider-style loader (user-removable, removal sticky).
Area: extensions
Files: chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.{h,cc} (CreateExternalProviders at .h:58 and .cc:703); src-overlay/corvid/extensions/ (new loader)
Rebase risk: medium
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)
Status: SPEC (exact edits from the VM builder's read-only greps on 155.0.8059.39, relayed 2026-10-13). Still NO diff hunks and the edits are not applied or built. Generate the diff on the tree with scripts/refresh-patches.sh.

Tree findings (reported by the VM builder, read-only; not re-checked):
- ExternalProviderImpl and ExternalPrefLoader live in chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.{h,cc}; related: preinstalled_extensions.cc, extension_management.cc, extension_migrator.cc.
- Still to grep: ExternalProviderImpl::CreateExternalProviders (hook point and arguments), the 'uninstalled external extensions' pref (ExtensionPrefs::IsExternalExtensionUninstalled), the external-extension install flags (Manifest::EXTERNAL_PREF, whether user may disable/remove), and whether non-store (self-hosted CRX/update URL) installs need the update URL allowlist from extension_management.cc.

Change (exact edits):
1. Add corvid::PreinstalledExtensionsLoader in src-overlay/corvid/extensions/ as a subclass of ExternalLoader (reads the JSON emitted from extensions/preinstalled.toml; src-overlay/corvid/extensions/preinstalled_extensions.cc is the intended reader, confirm it exists before use).
2. In ExternalProviderImpl::CreateExternalProviders(VisitorInterface* service, Profile* profile, ProviderCollection* provider_list) (external_provider_impl.cc:703) append one ExternalProviderImpl built on the new loader to provider_list, location EXTERNAL_PREF (so the user can disable/uninstall), creation flags without FROM_BOOKMARK/WAS_INSTALLED_BY_DEFAULT only if the grep of Extension::InitFromValueFlags shows they are needed for uBO to be removable.
3. Sticky removal: no new code. The existing pref extensions.external_uninstalls (extension_prefs.cc:217) is written on uninstall and read via ExtensionPrefs::IsExternalExtensionUninstalled (used at extension_registrar.cc:1080, pending_extension_manager.cc:181, extension_prefs.cc:1499), so a removed uBO stays removed.
4. Add the loader's BUILD.gn dep; header include in external_provider_impl.cc.
5. Constructor (second grep round, Azure VM tree, line numbers +/-2): ExternalProviderImpl(VisitorInterface* service, scoped_refptr<ExternalLoader> loader, Profile* profile, mojom::ManifestLocation crx_location, mojom::ManifestLocation download_location, int creation_flags) at external_provider_impl.h:45-50 / .cc:146-152; body is DCHECK(profile_); loader_->Init(this). Model the new call on the existing one at .cc:927-934 (kExternalPref, kExternalPrefDownload, FROM_WEBSTORE | WAS_INSTALLED_BY_DEFAULT). Use kExternalPref / kExternalPrefDownload and WAS_INSTALLED_BY_DEFAULT; drop FROM_WEBSTORE only if uBO is installed from a non-store CRX (decide with the pin: extensions/preinstalled.toml).
6. Update URL: the provider has no update-URL restriction. extension_management.cc GetEffectiveUpdateURL (:259-276) only changes the URL when policy sets override_update_url (DCHECK at :274 against the webstore URL), so Corvid sets no such policy. Not traced: the CRX update path beyond that (how a non-store, self-hosted update URL is fetched and verified); check before claiming uBO updates work (acceptance 07).

